# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for `make test/tsan`.
#
# GDAL takes two of its own internal mutexes in both orders during startup
# (CPLCreateOrAcquireMutexEx / CPLAcquireMutex), on the main thread and before
# demd starts a single worker: `-t 1` reports it too. GDAL is not built with
# TSan, so this is not something demd can fix or even see into; suppressing it
# by library keeps any inversion involving demd's own locks reportable.
deadlock:libgdal.so
